{% doc %}
  Hands an email to whichever provider the instance is configured for.

  This is the seam the build spec asks for. Ticket logic never knows which
  provider is in use: it builds an email and calls this, and adding a
  second provider is one new file beside sendgrid plus a line here.

  Always returns { sent, status, provider_message_id }, including when
  nothing was sent, so the caller can record what actually happened rather
  than assuming.

  @param {object} object - to, cc, from_address, from_name, reply_to, subject, body, message_id, in_reply_to, references
  @param {object} settings - The settings record
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign provider = settings.provider | default: 'sendgrid'

  case provider
    when 'sendgrid'
      function result = 'modules/support/commands/outbound/sendgrid', object: object
      return result
    else
      log provider, type: 'ERROR: modules/support/commands/outbound/send does not know this provider'
      assign result = { "sent": false, "status": "unknown_provider", "provider_message_id": null }
      return result
  endcase
%}
